Navigation note (covenant #7 — no predecessor bypass): the web routes /analytics/anomalies and /anomaly-detection
are NEW destinations. The native AppRoute already has a `.diagnostics` case (operations group, stethoscope icon)
that was PREVIOUSLY UNHOSTED (no registration claimed it; the shell rendered its pending state) and corresponds to
no other web page (web has no /diagnostics route). The parity unit is itself `page:diagnostics/AnomalyDashboard`, so
hosting AnomalyDashboardPage at `.diagnostics` makes the existing Diagnostics sidebar entry functional WITHOUT
adding an enum case or displacing any sibling (.analytics still owns StatisticsPage; .tco still owns TrueCostPage).
AppRouteParser gains the two web-path aliases so both deep-links resolve. No AppRoute enum case, sibling
registration, or RouteTests invariant (unique pathSegments) was touched. The @Observable model is built @MainActor
in the registration enum and captured, mirroring the sibling *RouteRegistration enums.

UNITS / SSE note: this page renders only dimensionless data (signal counts, z-scores, raw signal value/baseline)
— the web page imports fmtNumber and NOT useUnits, and uses a TanStack query (no EventSource). So there is no SI
conversion and no live-staleness indicator to implement; AnomalyFormat handles the number/relative-time boundary.

